<title>FRANCE: EU sells wheat, flour to Afghanistan as food aid.</title>
<headline>EU sells wheat, flour to Afghanistan as food aid.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has agreed to ship 22,000 tonnes of soft wheat and 5,300 tonnes of soft wheat flour to Afghanistan via the World Food Programme under a food aid tender it held on December 17, France's grain office ONIC said on Monday.</p>
<p>The wheat was sold at 124.92 Ecus per tonne and the flour at 200.90 Ecus, it said.</p>
<p>Other EU food aid shipments agreed on December 17 included: (Prices in Ecus per tonne)</p>
<p>    Product	Tonnage    Destination		    Price</p>
<p>    Wheat flour    910 T    Euronaid Prg for Haiti,    196.77</p>
<p>				    Somalia, Madagascar</p>
<p>    White rice   2,160 T    Euronaid Prg for Haiti     253.00</p>
<p>    Maize	  8,800 T    Angola			   210.90</p>
<p>    Maize	  2,200 T    Angola			   210.90</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
